<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Manukyan et al. (2017) Nature hexagonal skin-scale border thickness reduction & outer-totalistic cellular automaton — 3D skin-volume reaction-diffusion (Pass 3) (Ocellated / jeweled lizard (Timon lepidus) dorsal skin scale labyrinth)",
        "Manukyan et al. (2017) Nature hexagonal skin-scale border thickness reduction & outer-totalistic cellular automaton — 3D skin-volume reaction-diffusion (Pass 3) faithfully reproduces Ocellated / jeweled lizard (Timon lepidus) dorsal skin scale labyrinth morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ocellated / jeweled lizard (Timon lepidus) dorsal skin scale labyrinth specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 83.6/100, audit 2026-10-19-ocellated-lizard-ca-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bd54e11/2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py> ;
    schema:about "Ocellated / jeweled lizard (Timon lepidus) dorsal skin scale labyrinth" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Reproduction of the paper's exact PDE parameters, a micro-CT skin mesh, domain growth, derivation of the CA flip probabilities from the PDE time series, or a neighbour-histogram match to Manukyan Fig. 3 beyond the vendored target vectors",
        "reconstructed_in_script: A genuine 3D finite-volume voxel reaction-diffusion solver on a stepped-thickness skin volume (12 interior voxels, dz = 0.2 px, h_border = round(P*12)) with zero-flux surfaces and an implicit vertical solve; its depth-averaged thin-film 2D reduction (1/h) div(h D grad u) with min(h_i, h_j) D face conductances; a leak-proof hexagonal scale geometry; Turing linear stability (d_c, k_c, lambda_c, unstable band) for the script kinetics and for the vendored canonical set; a 5-regime P sweep in 3D and 2D; insulated / equal-diffusion / continuum controls; the stochastic hexagonal outer-totalistic CA; chromatic segmentation of 182 dorsal scales on a SHA-256-pinned Timon lepidus photograph; 16 measurements and 14 self-test checks",
        "reported_in_source: Fofonjka & Milinkovitch (2021): reaction-diffusion in a growing 3D skin-scale domain with thin inter-scale borders generates the discrete cellular automaton",
        "reported_in_source: Manukyan et al. (2017): skin thickness at inter-scale borders is reduced to P = h_border/h_interior ~ 0.17; a Kondo-Asai reaction-diffusion system on this geometry homogenises within scales and reduces to a hexagonal outer-totalistic cellular automaton whose adult neighbour histogram peaks at n_g = 3 (Figs. 2-4)",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952): diffusion-driven instability requires tr J < 0, det J > 0, d f_u + g_v > 2 sqrt(d det J)",
        "transfer_boundary: The 3D domain is a stepped voxel skin on a 5 px scale pitch (border area fraction 0.36, no domain growth), not the micro-CT-derived finite-element geometry of Fofonjka & Milinkovitch (2021); the reaction kinetics (f_u = 0.50, f_v = -0.75, g_u = 0.82, g_v = -0.65, cubic 1.25) are a phenomenological Kondo-Asai-type set, not the Methods parameters of Manukyan et al. (2017)",
        "transfer_boundary: The CA transition probabilities and adult histogram targets in ocellated_lizard_ca_reference.json carry no digitisation provenance to a specific figure/table; the 'canonical' clipped-linear parameter set in the same file is not Turing-unstable at its stated d = 20 (d_c = 23.57) and is not used by the solvers",
        "transfer_boundary: The specimen comparison samples a fixed 13 x 14 hexagonal lattice over the dorsal ROI rather than detecting scale centres, so neighbour statistics inherit lattice-registration error" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Amphibia & Reptilia (Ootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Timon" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bd54e11/2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py; output: docs/media/ocellated_lizard_ca_comparison.png; organism: Ocellated / jeweled lizard (Timon lepidus) dorsal skin scale labyrinth; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/bd54e11; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 46cc2c30ccba89108a6a17ed5177834284431b172cd845c2faca9279833944dd; artifact_sha256: f3a39c7c6dedb783fd81cb698c652481d6057844e19017873d6e0f82d7c76b4e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ocellated_lizard_ca/ocellated_lizard_ca_reference.json=53832b76e25303a6..., datasets/ocellated_lizard_ca/scout_manifest.json=e5bca2d8766b49e7..., datasets/ocellated_lizard_ca/skin_volume_reference.json=dc8da9f0b72dad3a..., datasets/ocellated_lizard_ca/timon_lepidus_specimen.jpg=bc8e149849e6729d...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-ocellated-lizard-ca-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Manukyan et al. (2017): skin thickness at inter-scale borders is reduced to P = h_border/h_interior ~ 0.17; a Kondo-Asai reaction-diffusion system on this geometry homogenises within scales and reduces to a hexagonal outer-totalistic cellular automaton whose adult neighbour histogram peaks at n_g = 3 (Figs. 2-4) | Fofonjka & Milinkovitch (2021): reaction-diffusion in a growing 3D skin-scale domain with thin inter-scale borders generates the discrete cellular automaton | Turing (1952): diffusion-driven instability requires tr J < 0, det J > 0, d f_u + g_v > 2 sqrt(d det J); reconstructed_in_script: A genuine 3D finite-volume voxel reaction-diffusion solver on a stepped-thickness skin volume (12 interior voxels, dz = 0.2 px, h_border = round(P*12)) with zero-flux surfaces and an implicit vertical solve; its depth-averaged thin-film 2D reduction (1/h) div(h D grad u) with min(h_i, h_j) D face conductances; a leak-proof hexagonal scale geometry; Turing linear stability (d_c, k_c, lambda_c, unstable band) for the script kinetics and for the vendored canonical set; a 5-regime P sweep in 3D and 2D; insulated / equal-diffusion / continuum controls; the stochastic hexagonal outer-totalistic CA; chromatic segmentation of 182 dorsal scales on a SHA-256-pinned Timon lepidus photograph; 16 measurements and 14 self-test checks; transfer_boundary: The 3D domain is a stepped voxel skin on a 5 px scale pitch (border area fraction 0.36, no domain growth), not the micro-CT-derived finite-element geometry of Fofonjka & Milinkovitch (2021); the reaction kinetics (f_u = 0.50, f_v = -0.75, g_u = 0.82, g_v = -0.65, cubic 1.25) are a phenomenological Kondo-Asai-type set, not the Methods parameters of Manukyan et al. (2017) | The CA transition probabilities and adult histogram targets in ocellated_lizard_ca_reference.json carry no digitisation provenance to a specific figure/table; the 'canonical' clipped-linear parameter set in the same file is not Turing-unstable at its stated d = 20 (d_c = 23.57) and is not used by the solvers | The specimen comparison samples a fixed 13 x 14 hexagonal lattice over the dorsal ROI rather than detecting scale centres, so neighbour statistics inherit lattice-registration error; does_not_claim: Reproduction of the paper's exact PDE parameters, a micro-CT skin mesh, domain growth, derivation of the CA flip probabilities from the PDE time series, or a neighbour-histogram match to Manukyan Fig. 3 beyond the vendored target vectors]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature22031>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-021-22525-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevX.13.041011> ;
