<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Manukyan et al. (2017) Nature hexagonal skin-scale border thickness reduction & outer-totalistic cellular automaton — 3D skin-volume reaction-diffusion (Pass 3) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-85) maps each solver to its source and states the Pass 3 remediation and its limits; every PDE function docstring gives the governing equation it discretises (L630-646, L748-772), the border definition explains why the v2 band leaked (L461-470), the Lean theorems are cross-referenced from the code and registered with code loci in `morphoeval/math_kg_loops/manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.yaml` (laws 1-5), and measurement notes say which v2 number was an artefact. Deductions: the kinetics constants (L332) and the CA damping factor 0.35 (L296-297) are not traced to any equation or figure (-6); the 55th percentile threshold used for both PDE scales and the specimen (L594, L1012) is an unexplained choice (-4); the `reference_value` anchors 3.5 and 4.0 are documented as choices only in the measurement text (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py L296–L297: CA asynchronous damping factor 0.35 is uncited <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bd54e11/2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py#L296-L297>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Manukyan et al. (2017) Nature hexagonal skin-scale border thickness reduction & outer-totalistic cellular automaton — 3D skin-volume reaction-diffusion (Pass 3) — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The code now implements the mechanism the papers describe: reaction-diffusion in a 3D skin volume whose thickness drops to P h_interior at scale borders (`integrate_skin_volume_pde_3d`, L739-865: voxel mask z < h(x,y), skin-skin face conductances, zero-flux steps, implicit Thomas vertical solve L720-736), the depth-averaged reduction with the correct h-weighted conductance and capacity (L616-717), a border definition through which all inter-scale flux passes (L450-536), and the mesoscopic premise that lambda_c = 5 pitches exceeds the scale so isolated scales cannot pattern (L325-443, measured: insulated inter std 5e-3, intra std 8e-9). The v2 averaging hack is gone and the paper's qualitative result emerges from the geometry alone (P = 0.17 ratio 14.7 vs continuum 3.29). Deductions: the kinetics are a phenomenological set, not Manukyan's Methods parameters (L326-341) (-6); the domain is a stepped voxel skin without growth, not the 3D geometry of Fofonjka & Milinkovitch (-5); the CA flip probabilities are vendored tables rather than derived from the PDE as the paper does (L276-278) (-4); the PDE neighbour histogram peaks at n_g = 2, not 3 (L1 to CA 0.34) (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py L326–L341: Script kinetics constants 0.50/-0.75/0.82/-0.65/1.25 are phenomenological (Kondo-Asai-type), not the Methods parameters of Manukyan et al. (2017) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bd54e11/2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py#L326-L341>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Manukyan et al. (2017) Nature hexagonal skin-scale border thickness reduction & outer-totalistic cellular automaton — 3D skin-volume reaction-diffusion (Pass 3) — Morphometric validation: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1354-1537) returns 16 measurements with reference values and units: CA and specimen neighbour statistics against the vendored Fig. 3 targets, 3D discretization ratio and Ashman D, 3D-vs-2D scale-state agreement (0.903 vs 1.0), depth-averaged RMS (0.118), vertical non-uniformity (0.022), voxel volume fraction vs analytic (0.700 vs 0.700), insulated and equal-diffusion controls, P-sweep monotonicity (rho = -1.0), lambda_c in pitches (5.0) and the canonical set's d_c (23.57 vs its stated 20). Deductions: only two measurements are made on a real specimen (green fraction 0.4505 vs 0.44; <n_g> 2.60 vs 2.665) and the 0.44 / 2.665 targets have no digitisation provenance (-8); the 3.5 discretization-ratio reference and the 4.0-pitch lambda_c reference are assessor-chosen anchors, not values reported in the papers (-6); several references are self-consistency targets (agreement 1.0, RMS 0, volume fraction analytic) (-4); no uncertainty / seed ensemble is reported (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py L1398–L1407: 3D discretization ratio measurement references 3.5 — an anchor carried from Pass 1, not a value in Manukyan 2017 / Fofonjka 2021 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bd54e11/2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py#L1398-L1407>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-measurement-3d-skin-volume-pde-p-0-17-inter-to-intra-scale-concentration-discretization-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-measurement-3d-skin-volume-pde-p-0-17-scale-color-bimodality-ashman-s-d>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-measurement-3d-skin-volume-pde-vs-outer-totalistic-ca-neighbor-histogram-l1-distance>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-measurement-3d-skin-volume-vertical-non-uniformity-of-activator-rms-over-depth-interior-columns-p-0-17>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-measurement-3d-skin-volume-vs-depth-averaged-2d-reduction-rms-difference-of-depth-averaged-activator-p-0-17>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-measurement-3d-skin-volume-vs-depth-averaged-2d-thin-film-reduction-binary-scale-state-agreement-p-0-17>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-measurement-3d-skin-voxel-volume-fraction-relative-to-a-uniform-slab-p-0-17>,
